00:42:30.981 --> 00:42:33.250
It was a nice trip to Carrara

00:42:33.250 --> 00:42:36.253
A little holiday.

00:42:36.387 --> 00:42:39.390
It's a beautiful drive down Liguria.

00:42:39.523 --> 00:42:42.826
You reach Genoa,
and then you're at the Mediterranean Sea.

00:42:44.361 --> 00:42:45.663
beautiful, sunny days.

00:42:45.663 --> 00:42:48.632
And I went off the toll road
a few times 

00:42:49.033 --> 00:42:52.236
to see the countryside. It goes very slow
because the roads go...

00:42:53.170 --> 00:42:56.740
The hills are very steep
there, but it's incredibly beautiful.

00:42:58.242 --> 00:43:01.745
Then you reach Carrara, which is just in Tuscany.

00:43:02.012 --> 00:43:04.782
It's about 3.5 hours from here.

00:43:04.782 --> 00:43:07.785
But with Fabio, who's...

00:43:08.252 --> 00:43:09.820
You might have seen him in the videos
here.

00:43:09.820 --> 00:43:12.156
He was helping us in October,

00:43:12.156 --> 00:43:15.159
when we were carrying the beams
up as part of the team

00:43:15.926 --> 00:43:18.062
And, he studied there,

00:43:18.062 --> 00:43:21.065
so he's well-connected.

00:43:21.198 --> 00:43:24.201
So he invited me and,

00:43:24.335 --> 00:43:28.706
introduced me to some artists and sculptors.

00:43:28.806 --> 00:43:32.242
I'll share a link of their art collective
in the in the description.

00:43:32.743 --> 00:43:36.046
It's interesting
to see how it works with marble.

00:43:36.080 --> 00:43:39.516
I mean, I've got some experience with
Stone now here, but it's quite different.

00:43:42.453 --> 00:43:43.120
The Luserna stone...

00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:46.290
which is this stone, it's
much harder and more brittle.

00:43:46.290 --> 00:43:49.293
So it's more difficult
to cut, easier to hammer.

00:43:50.027 --> 00:43:52.396
So here it's just used for

00:43:52.396 --> 00:43:54.732
structural purposes, like roofs and walls.

00:43:54.732 --> 00:43:58.369
But marble obviously is used
for so many other things.

00:43:59.069 --> 00:44:01.905
And Carrara, it's
where it's at, you know, it's where

00:44:03.273 --> 00:44:03.807
I'm not sure

00:44:03.807 --> 00:44:06.810
if most of the marble comes from there,
but historically it does.

00:44:09.213 --> 00:44:10.814
Michelangelo's David,

00:44:10.814 --> 00:44:13.817
the block of marble, for example,
comes from there.

00:44:14.018 --> 00:44:17.421
So there was a lot of history
interesting to learn about it. And,

00:44:18.956 --> 00:44:22.459
interesting to meet the people, stayed in hotel, everything is made of marble.

00:44:22.459 --> 00:44:25.462
Very beautiful.

00:44:25.829 --> 00:44:28.465
I'm looking forward to, to work with it,

00:44:28.465 --> 00:44:33.203
although I have no experience, I have to learn everything, but it's a bit easier

00:44:33.203 --> 00:44:36.206
to work with this stone,
so that's probably

00:44:36.206 --> 00:44:39.209
a job for, what, next year or so?

00:44:40.044 --> 00:44:42.746
Because it's really the last job
I will do on the kitchen

00:44:42.746 --> 00:44:45.749
and the bathroom.

00:44:46.316 --> 00:44:48.652
So yeah,

00:44:48.652 --> 00:44:50.587
sun's coming through again.

00:44:50.587 --> 00:44:52.723
Beautiful week.

00:44:52.723 --> 00:44:54.458
It's not spring yet.

00:44:54.458 --> 00:44:55.426
It's going to snow again.

00:44:55.426 --> 00:44:57.194
I think tomorrow, and tonight

00:44:59.129 --> 00:45:00.464
Here it’s still a lot of snow

00:45:00.464 --> 00:45:03.934
